te" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)=⌊-3x+1⌋+6,$ then $f(1.5)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =⌊-3(1.5)+1⌋+6 \\\\  & =⌊-4.5+1⌋+6 \\\\  & =⌊-3.5⌋+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-3.5⌋=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =⌊-3.5⌋+6 \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182042" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.ty