nk "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182039" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=x⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡(8x+1)+1⌋$ at $x=3.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=3.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.5) & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡(8\\cdot 3.5+1)+1⌋ \\\\  & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋=⌊2.462\\,39…⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.5) & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋ \\\\  & =3.5(2) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=x⌊{e}^{x+1}⌋$ at $x=0.75.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75⌊{e}^{0.75+1}⌋ \\\\  & =0.75⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋=⌊5.754\\,60…⌋=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋ \\\\  & =0.75(5) \\\\  & =3.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3.25"] ["math" "3.50"] ["math" "3.75"] ["math" "4.25"] ["math" "4.50"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.75"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)⌋$ at $x=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡(11+2)⌋ \\\\  & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋=⌊2.564\\,94…⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋ \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{⌊{x}^{3}⌋}{{x}^{2}}$ at $x=-2.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-2.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{⌊(-2.5)^{3}⌋}{(-2.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⌊-15.625⌋}{6.25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊-15.625⌋=-16.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{⌊-15.625⌋}{6.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-16)}{6.25} \\\\  & =-2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2.12"] ["math" "-2.25"] ["math" "-2.56"] ["math" "2.15"] ["math" "2.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.56"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{⌊1-x⌋}}{x}$ at $x=-1.5.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊1-(-1.5)⌋}}{(-1.5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊1+1.5⌋}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.5⌋}}{1.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊2.5⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.5⌋}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-4.926\\,03… \\\\  & ≈-4.93,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-41915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-41915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.25"] ["math" "-13.39"] ["math" "-4.93"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "13.39"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d