"answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)=3-⌈1+5x⌉,$ then $f(1.6)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.6) & =3-⌈1+5(1.6)⌉ \\\\  & =3-⌈1+8⌉ \\\\  & =3-⌈9⌉\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈9⌉=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.6) & =3-⌈9⌉ \\\\  & =3-9 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182053" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake