uestion" "q-182121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "19"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=x+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(8x+1)⌉$ at $x=9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(8\\cdot 9+1)⌉ \\\\  & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(72+1)⌉ \\\\  & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉=⌈1.863\\,32…⌉=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉ \\\\  & =9+2 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "16"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=⌈x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4)⌉$ at $x=5.7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=5.7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5.7) & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5.7-4)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉=⌈3.024\\,58……⌉=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5.7) & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉ \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{{3}^{⌈5x-2⌉}}{x}$ at $x=0.7.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.7) & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈5(0.7)-2⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈3.5-2⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈1.5⌉}}{0.7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈1.5⌉=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.7) & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈1.5⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{0.7} \\\\  & =12.857\\,14… \\\\  & ≈12.86,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11.97"] ["math" "12.05"] ["math" "12.86"] ["math" "13.34"] ["math" "13.78"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12.86"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}+1)⌉$ at $x=-2.3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-2.3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.3) & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((-2.3)^{4}+1)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(27.984\\,1+1)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉=⌈-3.366\\,74…⌉=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.3) & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉ \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e252ad2a8fcb16d8d06f44fc721f38ca80ec2e25cb9cdb7ba1081ffe2e87696"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "q-182127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/state.json" "file_sha256" "a45e43011ed67c819960aa8ccc1e890eefc586d7fa064e9f2d11a5f766d07d53"} {"question" "e-6017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)=2x+\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{x}{5} \\right\\rfloor,$ then what is the value of $f(-0.5)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-6017.json" "file_sha256" "a3ba86545055ba10e390e932d70cf4a963ee5f6eb19cb2ead2ab3fab523a631b"} {"question" "e-6017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =2\\cdot (-0.5)+⌊\\frac{-0.5}{5}⌋ \\\\  & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-0.1⌋=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋ \\\\  & =-1+(-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-6017.json" "file_sha256" "a3ba86545055ba10e390e932d70cf4a963ee5f6eb19cb2ead2ab3fab523a631b"} {"question" "e-13202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x) = \\dfrac{e^{\\left\\lfloor x+2 \\right\\rfloor}}{2x+1}$ at $x = 0.75.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-13202.json" "file_sha256" "ae9dd36a5db07f29bf24e33c98ec3225d0e3a08fadcaecf0865bfa6e3d36e57c"} {"question" "e-13202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊0.75+2⌋}}{2(0.75)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2.5} \\\\  & =2.955\\,62… \\\\  & ≈2.96,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-13202.json" "file_sha256" "ae9dd36a5db07f29bf24e33c98ec3225d0e3a08fadcaecf0865bfa6e3d36e57c"} {"question" "e-6022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x)=(\\lceil 6x-3 \\rceil -2)^3$ at $x=0.4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-6022.json" "file_sha256" "648bbd4861791599b62007a648473c1d9d076a27d399bf6e84b5f6d82dd3d656"} {"question" "e-6022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈6(0.4)-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈2.4-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\lceil -0.6 \\rceil = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{3} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-6022.json" "file_sha256" "648bbd4861791599b62007a648473c1d9d076a27d399bf6e84b5f6d82dd3d656"} {"question" "e-13203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $f(x) = \\left \\lceil e^{6x-5} \\right \\rceil$ at $x = 1.25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-13203.json" "file_sha256" "4ee94076827ebfacb5a1e7a7c1927b0ca874beb223ecb62d053ab12f5e131af8"} {"question" "e-13203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 1.25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{6(1.25)-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{7.5-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left \\lceil e^{2.5} \\right \\rceil = \\left \\lceil 12.182\\,49 \\ldots \\right \\rceil = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉ \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-13203.json" "file_sha256" "4ee94076827ebfacb5a1e7a7c1927b0ca874beb223ecb62d053ab12f5e131af8"}] "usage" {"e-13203" [] "e-6022" [] "e-6017" [] "q-182107" [] "e-13202" []} "basis" 1248 "retractions" [[17592186064448 :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x) = ⌊\\ln (x + 2)⌋$ at $x = 11$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186064025 :question/problem "If $f(x)=2x+\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{x}{5} \\right\\rfloor$, then what is the value of $f(-0.5)$?"] [17592186064025 :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-0.5) &= 2 \\cdot (-0.5) + ⌊\\frac{-0.5}{5}⌋ \\\\\n&=-1 + ⌊ - 0.1⌋\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n⌊ - 0.1⌋ =-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-0.5) &= -1 + ⌊ - 0.1⌋ \\\\\n&=-1 + (-1) \\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063865 :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x) = \\dfrac{e^{\\left\\lfloor x+2 \\right\\rfloor}}{2x+1}$ at $x = 0.75$. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186063865 :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.75) &= (e^{⌊0.75 + 2⌋})/(2(0.75) + 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.75) &= \\frac{e^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{2}}{2.5} \\\\\n&= 2.95562… \\\\\n&\\approx 2.96\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186064026 :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=(\\lceil 6x-3 \\rceil -2)^3$ at $x=0.4$."] [17592186064026 :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.4) &= (⌈6(0.4) - 3⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (⌈2.4 - 3⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (⌈ - 0.6⌉ - 2)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\lceil -0.6 \\rceil = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.4) &= (⌈ - 0.6⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (0 - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (-2)^{3} \\\\\n&=-8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063866 :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x) = \\left \\lceil e^{6x-5} \\right \\rceil$ at $x = 1.25$."] [17592186063866 :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 1.25$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1.25) &= ⌈e^{6(1.25) - 5}⌉ \\\\\n&= ⌈e^{7.5 - 5}⌉ \\\\\n&= ⌈e^{2.5}⌉\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left \\lceil e^{2.5} \\right \\rceil = \\left \\lceil 12.182\\,49 \\ldots \\right \\rceil = 13\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1.25) &= ⌈e^{2.5}⌉ \\\\\n&= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061338 17592186061339 17592186061340 17592186061341 17592186061342] "immutable_fields" [[17592186061337 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061337 :answer-field/id] [17592186061337 :answer-field/key] [17592186061337 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
